    <h1>{{ talk.project.title }}</h1>
    <p class="lede">This talk starts from a simple claim: authentication keeps failing not because people ignore advice, but because the system asks too much of them.</p>
    <p>Password managers and MFA help, but phishing and credential theft remain common because reusable secrets are still part of the design. Passkeys change that shape by replacing shared secrets with public-key proof.</p>
    <p>Use this site as the reference version of the session: revisit the argument, follow the examples, and take the standards and implementation links with you.</p>
